#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1445
msgid "A rush of real visitors (a newsletter, a link on a popular site) looks the same as an attack. Emergency Mode changes many settings at once, listed in its box on the first tab, e.g. excerpts instead of full text in lists and stricter limits for data centers, where some services in “Always allowed” run. Feeds stay open to feed readers and podcast apps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1448
msgid "Minimum pages per minute for the automatic start:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1448
msgid "Below this the site is never considered under attack, however quiet it usually is. Starting value: 300 (5 pages per second)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1453
msgid "A small script waits for the visitor's first real interaction (scroll, tap, key or mouse movement), solves a light challenge in the background and receives a cookie for 7 days. Nobody sees a captcha or a window. Visitors without the cookie (scripts, and people with JavaScript turned off) get the limit below instead of the normal page limit. Search engines and verified AI search bots are not affected. With a page cache plugin, turn on the pre-cache check so that cached pages get this limit too. A determined scraper can repeat the steps, but each of its IPs has to do the work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1454
msgid "Pages per minute without the cookie (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1454
msgid "Starting value: 20. A person reads far fewer pages per minute, and gets the cookie with the first scroll or tap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1460
msgid "Each IP gets a score from what it did here in the last 7 days, recent events counting more: someone signed in from it, it passed the human check, it reads pages (good); the bot trap, a scanner probe, a fake search engine, an attack in the request, limits exceeded, a temporary block (bad). An IP with a good score (someone signed in and passed the human check) is never blocked temporarily for exceeding a limit: it still gets “too many requests”, but an office, a school or a mobile network behind one address is not locked out because of one fast reader. An IP with a bad score gets the stricter limit below for days, instead of starting from zero when its block ends. Stored like the per-minute counters; no data leaves the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1461
msgid "Pages per minute for IPs with a bad reputation (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1461
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1469
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1506
