msgid "For visitors who are not signed in: everything “Hide the versions” below does, plus no REST API, oEmbed, RSD and shortlink links in the page head and headers, no emoji script, no X-Pingback and “X-Redirect-By: WordPress” headers. Tools such as BuiltWith and Wappalyzer, and scanners, look for these first. Everything keeps working. It cannot hide everything: the addresses of themes and plugins (/wp-content/…) still show it, and the hosting and DNS of a site are public anyway. Add the Nginx or Apache rules (Server rules tab) to refuse readme.html and license.txt too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1993
msgid "Hide the versions of WordPress, PHP and the plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1993
msgid "Scanners read these versions and look them up in lists of known vulnerabilities. This removes the “generator” tag from the page head and the feeds, the X-Powered-By header with the PHP version, and replaces “?ver=7.1.3” on CSS and JS files with a code that changes when the version changes, so caches still work. The readme and changelog files of WordPress and the plugins are static files: the Nginx and Apache rules in the “Server rules” tab refuse them. It does not fix any vulnerability: keep WordPress and the plugins updated."
msgstr ""

